* ---- cx100p / cx1n: the PRACTICAL form of a low sampling-instant source
* impedance -- DR-0001's contracted 500 ohm series source with an external
* shunt capacitor at the input pin (the standard ADC-driver kickback
* network, and the same external-component idiom DR-0002 already uses for
* V_REF decoupling). The DC source impedance is unchanged at 500 ohm; what
* changes is the impedance the injected charge sees on the 1 ns turn-off
* edge, which is set by C_ext (dt/C = 10 ohm at 100 pF, 1 ohm at 1 nF), not
* by the resistor. rd stays at the as-drawn 1:2. ----------------------------
Rs_cx100p_f00 nin_f00 ni_cx100p_f00 500
Cx_cx100p_f00 ni_cx100p_f00 0 100p
Xsw_cx100p_f00 ni_cx100p_f00 no_cx100p_f00 nclk nclkb vdd tgate_dum wn=40u wp=80u rd=0.5
XCl_cx100p_f00 no_cx100p_f00 0 mim_cap_2f0 c_width=66.36u c_length=66.36u
Rs_cx100p_f100 nin_f100 ni_cx100p_f100 500
Cx_cx100p_f100 ni_cx100p_f100 0 100p
Xsw_cx100p_f100 ni_cx100p_f100 no_cx100p_f100 nclk nclkb vdd tgate_dum wn=40u wp=80u rd=0.5
XCl_cx100p_f100 no_cx100p_f100 0 mim_cap_2f0 c_width=66.36u c_length=66.36u

Rs_cx1n_f00 nin_f00 ni_cx1n_f00 500
Cx_cx1n_f00 ni_cx1n_f00 0 1n
Xsw_cx1n_f00 ni_cx1n_f00 no_cx1n_f00 nclk nclkb vdd tgate_dum wn=40u wp=80u rd=0.5
XCl_cx1n_f00 no_cx1n_f00 0 mim_cap_2f0 c_width=66.36u c_length=66.36u
Rs_cx1n_f100 nin_f100 ni_cx1n_f100 500
Cx_cx1n_f100 ni_cx1n_f100 0 1n
Xsw_cx1n_f100 ni_cx1n_f100 no_cx1n_f100 nclk nclkb vdd tgate_dum wn=40u wp=80u rd=0.5
XCl_cx1n_f100 no_cx1n_f100 0 mim_cap_2f0 c_width=66.36u c_length=66.36u

* ---- cxopt: the candidate compliant configuration -- 25 ohm series source
* + 1 nF external shunt capacitor at the input pin (a standard ADC-driver RC
* network: 25 ohm x (1 nF + 8.83 pF) = 25 ns, ~12 tau inside the 300 ns track
* window, so the pin recovers from the sampling kick with margin) AND the
* dummy ratio re-tuned from the textbook 0.50 to 7/16 = 0.4375 (dummy
* 17.5u/35.0u -- 7 of the main device's 16 fingers, so the ratio is set by
* finger COUNT and the dummy is a literal replica slice of the main device,
* which is what makes it match).
*
* THE HYPOTHESIS THIS BRANCH TESTS. The s10..s150 sweep above shows the bare
* drive's split fraction is a strong function of Rs -- which is a user
* parameter DR-0001 leaves free anywhere in 0..500 ohm, so no fixed dummy
* ratio can null it. A shunt capacitor at the pin holds the source-side node
* rigid for the whole 1 ns turn-off edge, so the series resistance stops
* rate-limiting the charge that leaves through the source, and the split
* should stop depending on Rs. The cx100p/cx1n (Rs = 500) and cx100pl/cx1nl
* (Rs = 25) pairs measure exactly that, at the same rd, and cxopt/cxopth/
* cxoptl re-measure it at the re-tuned ratio across the whole allowed Rs
* range. NOTE this is NOT the naive "the split becomes the capacitor ratio
* C_hold/(C_hold+C_ext)" argument -- that would predict a split fraction of
* 0.009 at C_ext = 1 nF, and the measurement does not support it. -----------
Rs_cxopt_f00 nin_f00 ni_cxopt_f00 25
Cx_cxopt_f00 ni_cxopt_f00 0 1n
Xsw_cxopt_f00 ni_cxopt_f00 no_cxopt_f00 nclk nclkb vdd tgate_dum wn=40u wp=80u rd=0.4375
XCl_cxopt_f00 no_cxopt_f00 0 mim_cap_2f0 c_width=66.36u c_length=66.36u
Rs_cxopt_f25 nin_f25 ni_cxopt_f25 25
Cx_cxopt_f25 ni_cxopt_f25 0 1n
Xsw_cxopt_f25 ni_cxopt_f25 no_cxopt_f25 nclk nclkb vdd tgate_dum wn=40u wp=80u rd=0.4375
XCl_cxopt_f25 no_cxopt_f25 0 mim_cap_2f0 c_width=66.36u c_length=66.36u
Rs_cxopt_f50 nin_f50 ni_cxopt_f50 25
Cx_cxopt_f50 ni_cxopt_f50 0 1n
Xsw_cxopt_f50 ni_cxopt_f50 no_cxopt_f50 nclk nclkb vdd tgate_dum wn=40u wp=80u rd=0.4375
XCl_cxopt_f50 no_cxopt_f50 0 mim_cap_2f0 c_width=66.36u c_length=66.36u
Rs_cxopt_f75 nin_f75 ni_cxopt_f75 25
Cx_cxopt_f75 ni_cxopt_f75 0 1n
Xsw_cxopt_f75 ni_cxopt_f75 no_cxopt_f75 nclk nclkb vdd tgate_dum wn=40u wp=80u rd=0.4375
XCl_cxopt_f75 no_cxopt_f75 0 mim_cap_2f0 c_width=66.36u c_length=66.36u
Rs_cxopt_f100 nin_f100 ni_cxopt_f100 25
Cx_cxopt_f100 ni_cxopt_f100 0 1n
Xsw_cxopt_f100 ni_cxopt_f100 no_cxopt_f100 nclk nclkb vdd tgate_dum wn=40u wp=80u rd=0.4375
XCl_cxopt_f100 no_cxopt_f100 0 mim_cap_2f0 c_width=66.36u c_length=66.36u

* ---- cx100pl / cx1nl: the low-Rs half of the shunt-capacitor pair. Same
* rd = 0.5 as cx100p/cx1n, same C_ext, Rs = 25 ohm instead of 500 ohm. The
* cx100p/cx100pl and cx1n/cx1nl pairs are the controlled experiment: with rd
* and C_ext held fixed, any residual gain difference between the two members
* of a pair is what is LEFT of the drive dependence after C_ext pins the
* split. Compare against s20 vs tg4dum (the same 25x change in Rs with no
* shunt capacitor at all), which is the uncontrolled case. -----------------
Rs_cx100pl_f00 nin_f00 ni_cx100pl_f00 25
Cx_cx100pl_f00 ni_cx100pl_f00 0 100p
Xsw_cx100pl_f00 ni_cx100pl_f00 no_cx100pl_f00 nclk nclkb vdd tgate_dum wn=40u wp=80u rd=0.5
XCl_cx100pl_f00 no_cx100pl_f00 0 mim_cap_2f0 c_width=66.36u c_length=66.36u
Rs_cx100pl_f100 nin_f100 ni_cx100pl_f100 25
Cx_cx100pl_f100 ni_cx100pl_f100 0 100p
Xsw_cx100pl_f100 ni_cx100pl_f100 no_cx100pl_f100 nclk nclkb vdd tgate_dum wn=40u wp=80u rd=0.5
XCl_cx100pl_f100 no_cx100pl_f100 0 mim_cap_2f0 c_width=66.36u c_length=66.36u

Rs_cx1nl_f00 nin_f00 ni_cx1nl_f00 25
Cx_cx1nl_f00 ni_cx1nl_f00 0 1n
Xsw_cx1nl_f00 ni_cx1nl_f00 no_cx1nl_f00 nclk nclkb vdd tgate_dum wn=40u wp=80u rd=0.5
XCl_cx1nl_f00 no_cx1nl_f00 0 mim_cap_2f0 c_width=66.36u c_length=66.36u
Rs_cx1nl_f100 nin_f100 ni_cx1nl_f100 25
Cx_cx1nl_f100 ni_cx1nl_f100 0 1n
Xsw_cx1nl_f100 ni_cx1nl_f100 no_cx1nl_f100 nclk nclkb vdd tgate_dum wn=40u wp=80u rd=0.5
XCl_cx1nl_f100 no_cx1nl_f100 0 mim_cap_2f0 c_width=66.36u c_length=66.36u

* ---- cxopth: the CANDIDATE CONFIGURATION AT THE OTHER END OF THE ALLOWED
* SOURCE-IMPEDANCE RANGE. Identical to cxopt (C_ext = 1 nF, rd = 7/16) with
* Rs = 500 ohm -- DR-0001's contracted worst case -- instead of 25 ohm. This
* is the branch that decides whether the re-tuned dummy is a switch-level
* fix or only a fix at one drive point: a fixed dummy ratio is only
* defensible if this branch and cxopt read the same gain error. Full 5-level
* ladder so the nonlinearity and droop columns are available here too.
*
* CAVEAT, stated because this branch is easy to over-read: Rs = 500 ohm with
* C_ext = 1 nF gives the input PIN a 500 ns recovery time constant against a
* 300 ns track window, so this combination does NOT settle a moving input
* (see the record's drive-network derivation). It is measured here as a
* CHARGE-SPLIT control, at DC input levels where the priming cycle removes
* the settling term, not as a recommended drive network. ------------------
Rs_cxopth_f00 nin_f00 ni_cxopth_f00 500
Cx_cxopth_f00 ni_cxopth_f00 0 1n
Xsw_cxopth_f00 ni_cxopth_f00 no_cxopth_f00 nclk nclkb vdd tgate_dum wn=40u wp=80u rd=0.4375
XCl_cxopth_f00 no_cxopth_f00 0 mim_cap_2f0 c_width=66.36u c_length=66.36u
Rs_cxopth_f25 nin_f25 ni_cxopth_f25 500
Cx_cxopth_f25 ni_cxopth_f25 0 1n
Xsw_cxopth_f25 ni_cxopth_f25 no_cxopth_f25 nclk nclkb vdd tgate_dum wn=40u wp=80u rd=0.4375
XCl_cxopth_f25 no_cxopth_f25 0 mim_cap_2f0 c_width=66.36u c_length=66.36u
Rs_cxopth_f50 nin_f50 ni_cxopth_f50 500
Cx_cxopth_f50 ni_cxopth_f50 0 1n
Xsw_cxopth_f50 ni_cxopth_f50 no_cxopth_f50 nclk nclkb vdd tgate_dum wn=40u wp=80u rd=0.4375
XCl_cxopth_f50 no_cxopth_f50 0 mim_cap_2f0 c_width=66.36u c_length=66.36u
Rs_cxopth_f75 nin_f75 ni_cxopth_f75 500
Cx_cxopth_f75 ni_cxopth_f75 0 1n
Xsw_cxopth_f75 ni_cxopth_f75 no_cxopth_f75 nclk nclkb vdd tgate_dum wn=40u wp=80u rd=0.4375
XCl_cxopth_f75 no_cxopth_f75 0 mim_cap_2f0 c_width=66.36u c_length=66.36u
Rs_cxopth_f100 nin_f100 ni_cxopth_f100 500
Cx_cxopth_f100 ni_cxopth_f100 0 1n
Xsw_cxopth_f100 ni_cxopth_f100 no_cxopth_f100 nclk nclkb vdd tgate_dum wn=40u wp=80u rd=0.4375
XCl_cxopth_f100 no_cxopth_f100 0 mim_cap_2f0 c_width=66.36u c_length=66.36u

* ---- cxoptl: the candidate configuration at the BOTTOM of the allowed
* source-impedance range, Rs = 1 ohm (a hard driver right at the pin). The
* bare-drive s10 branch shows the split fraction is still moving fast at
* 10 ohm, so this is the branch that catches an over-compensated corner if
* C_ext does not in fact pin the split. -----------------------------------
Rs_cxoptl_f00 nin_f00 ni_cxoptl_f00 1
Cx_cxoptl_f00 ni_cxoptl_f00 0 1n
Xsw_cxoptl_f00 ni_cxoptl_f00 no_cxoptl_f00 nclk nclkb vdd tgate_dum wn=40u wp=80u rd=0.4375
XCl_cxoptl_f00 no_cxoptl_f00 0 mim_cap_2f0 c_width=66.36u c_length=66.36u
Rs_cxoptl_f100 nin_f100 ni_cxoptl_f100 1
Cx_cxoptl_f100 ni_cxoptl_f100 0 1n
Xsw_cxoptl_f100 ni_cxoptl_f100 no_cxoptl_f100 nclk nclkb vdd tgate_dum wn=40u wp=80u rd=0.4375
XCl_cxoptl_f100 no_cxoptl_f100 0 mim_cap_2f0 c_width=66.36u c_length=66.36u

